# Every JVM dispatch shape emit-jvm declines, classified. An NTS4009 is
# an override whose representation differs from the method it overrides: the JVM
# refuses it by name, and C and LLVM dispatch it without a check. So each shape is
# either the JVM's alone by construction, or live on C (and then a fixture shows
# it), or refused everywhere once lowering refuses it too, or owned and not yet
# measured. NTS4001 also names conflicting dispatch bodies at one JVM member
# and descriptor, which native tables can distinguish. jvm-verifies.ts fails
# on a dispatch shape not here.
# shape<TAB>verdict<TAB>why -- shapes are normalised (ClosureN, $N$, FnN, TypeN).
ChildWritable._write (Lnts/rt/NtsViewU8;Ljava/lang/String;Lnts/gen/erased/Callable;)V over (Lnts/rt/NtsValue;Ljava/lang/String;Lnts/gen/erased/Callable;)V	refused-everywhere	a narrowed parameter read at an erased argument: was SIGSEGV on C, refused by lowering since b09c3e6f6 -- a-writable-override-narrowing-an-erased-chunk (child_process, cluster)
PerformanceNodeEntry.toJSON ()Lnts/gen/PerformanceEntryDetailJSON; over ()Lnts/gen/PerformanceEntryJSON;	jvm-only	a covariant record that extends the base's: a-covariant-record-that-extends-the-base
PerformanceMark.toJSON ()Lnts/gen/PerformanceEntryDetailJSON; over ()Lnts/gen/PerformanceEntryJSON;	jvm-only	a covariant record that extends the base's: a-covariant-record-that-extends-the-base
PerformanceMeasure.toJSON ()Lnts/gen/PerformanceEntryDetailJSON; over ()Lnts/gen/PerformanceEntryJSON;	jvm-only	a covariant record that extends the base's: a-covariant-record-that-extends-the-base
PerformanceNodeTiming.toJSON ()Lnts/gen/PerformanceNodeTimingJSON; over ()Lnts/gen/PerformanceEntryJSON;	jvm-only	a covariant record repeating the base's fields in its order: a-covariant-record-that-repeats-the-base (reordered would be live: a-covariant-record-with-the-base-fields-reordered)
PerformanceResourceTiming.toJSON ()Lnts/gen/PerformanceResourceTimingJSON; over ()Lnts/gen/PerformanceEntryJSON;	jvm-only	a covariant record repeating the base's fields in its order: a-covariant-record-that-repeats-the-base
ClosureN.call (Lnts/gen/ReadableStreamDefaultController$N$;)V over (Lnts/gen/ReadableStreamDefaultController$N$;)V	jvm-only	TeeBranch's start closure storing a controller of another instantiation: one layout (a pointer), and a-controller-stored-by-a-generic-branch reproduces this decline and agrees on C; every site is unreachable today, TeeBranch#constructor being refused on its QueuingStrategy (a-teed-stream-read-back)
User.update (Lnts/gen/TypeN;)Ljava/lang/String; over (Lnts/rt/NtsValue;)Ljava/lang/String;	refused-everywhere	a narrowed parameter read at an erased argument: was SIGSEGV on C, refused by lowering since b09c3e6f6 -- an-override-reading-an-erased-argument (outcomes only; the React reconciler's shape)
ClosureN.call (Lnts/gen/Controller$N$;)V over (Lnts/gen/Controller$N$;)V	jvm-only	the reduction of TeeBranch's start closure: a-controller-stored-by-a-generic-branch agrees on C
dispatch conflict <any>.feed(Ljava/lang/String;)Lnts/rt/NtsValue;	jvm-only	two interface slots erase an absent string with different tags, regardless of class name; native tables distinguish them, but one JVM name and descriptor cannot (core/tests/programs/structural-absence)
dispatch conflict <any>.read(Ljava/lang/String;)Ljava/lang/String;	jvm-only	a stored literal erases null and undefined inputs differently for two interfaces; native tables keep separate bodies (a-literal-method-call-through-two-faces-loses-absence)
dispatch conflict <any>.read(Lnts/gen/erased/Callable;)D	jvm-only	a stored literal serves number and string callback interfaces through uniform calls; native tables preserve both projections (a-literal-interface-method-has-two-callback-contracts)

# Shared assignment checks now count storage refusals too. Each row's native
# behaviour was settled from the layouts (2026-10-11, the JVM lane): a store is
# jvm-only when C's read through the target is the source's own field -- same
# index, same type -- or the target has no field and no slot to read. A row
# stays unmeasured only where no program can reach the store on C.
stateful store TimersList -> ListNode	jvm-only	TimersList#constructor and append in http/fs; the target's fields sit at the same index and type in the source (nts layouts at 0c7055d82), so C's read through the target is the source's field
stateful store BlobTransportBodySource -> TransportBodySource	jvm-only	BodyState#transportBodySource in fs/http; the target's fields sit at the same index and type in the source (nts layouts at 0c7055d82), so C's read through the target is the source's field
stateful store MemoryHttpCacheBody -> HttpCacheBody	jvm-only	MemoryHttpCacheWriter#commit in fs/http; the target's fields sit at the same index and type in the source (nts layouts at 0c7055d82), so C's read through the target is the source's field
stateful store SystemErrorException -> SystemError	jvm-only	systemError and socketBufferError in fs/http; the target's fields sit at the same index and type in the source (nts layouts at 0c7055d82), so C's read through the target is the source's field
stateful store Immediate<N> -> ImmediateHandle	jvm-only	Immediate<N>#constructor; nine fields at one order, but _argv is Object(Args) in Immediate and Array(Erased) in ImmediateHandle (nts layouts at 0c7055d82). Through the handle _argv is only written, `immediate._argv = undefined` (timers/src/immediate.ts:210), the same null in both; read only as Immediate's own (:87). Live on C the day something reads _argv through the handle
stateful store UVHostPortError -> Error	jvm-only	dgram's return; the target's fields sit at the same index and type in the source (nts layouts at 0c7055d82), so C's read through the target is the source's field
stateful store DurableCacheEntry -> HttpCacheEntry	jvm-only	DurableHttpCacheStore#find newly declines an erased-array write; a-cache-entry-prefix-read-from-an-erased-array reproduces the baseline ClassCastException with extra entry fields, and agrees on C
unrelated store MemoryCacheStorageHandle -> EventTargetLike	jvm-only	MemoryCacheStorageStore#open/#lookup newly decline a Promise payload; an-opaque-promise-payload-read-as-an-unrelated-class reproduces the baseline ClassCastException on typed await (even discarded), and agrees on C
stateful store Reordered -> Shape	live-on-c	pre-existing JVM refusal at the callback; a-class-passed-to-a-callback-at-a-structural-type-in-another-field-order records C's reordered=300 against node's3
stateful store Ordered -> Shape	jvm-only	pre-existing JVM refusal at the same callback; the ordered control in a-class-passed-to-a-callback-at-a-structural-type-in-another-field-order agrees on C
unrelated store ReadableStreamAsyncIterator<N> -> Iterable<N>	unmeasured	pre-existing JVM refusal in a-teed-stream-read-back; not measurable on C from a program: `new ReadableStream` is NTS1001 (unrepresentable) in user code, and the fixture is refused before this iterator
stateful store ReadableStream<N> -> ReadableStream<N>	unmeasured	pre-existing JVM refusal in a-teed-stream-read-back; the four instantiations share one field order but each field is its own instantiation's layout (nts layouts at 0c7055d82), so a chunk type that differs is a real C confusion -- not measurable from a program while `new ReadableStream` is NTS1001 in user code
stateful store TypeN -> TypeN	jvm-only	pre-existing JVM generic-controller assignment refusal in a-controller-stored-by-a-generic-branch; that producer agrees on C
unrelated store ReadableStreamAsyncIterator<N> -> EventTargetLike	jvm-only	pre-existing JVM refusal in fs/http; the target is the merged empty layout (Iterable shares EventTargetLike's, nts layouts at 0c7055d82) with no field and no slot, so C reads nothing through it
unrelated store URLSearchParamsIteratorImpl -> EventTargetLike	jvm-only	pre-existing JVM refusal in fs/http/process; the target is the merged empty layout with no field and no slot (nts layouts at 0c7055d82), so C reads nothing through it
unrelated store URLSearchParamsIteratorImpl -> BlobExternalReader	jvm-only	pre-existing JVM refusal in url; the target is a merged empty layout with no field and no slot (nts layouts at 0c7055d82), so C reads nothing through it
